@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# MiniMax-M3.1 metadata pack
+
+This is the GGUF/DSpark metadata adapter for the separate MiniMax engine. It is adapted from
+Project Maya `26aacb6bcea9333e4f408a68ee60c4c1c316bd68` (MIT). Tensor mappings and model geometry
+come from Maya; bounded readers, path checks, complete-shard checks and atomic output are local.
+The model/template license is in `serve/fixtures/minimax_m31/LICENSE`.
+
+The pack references the existing files. It does not copy matrix weights or store runtime sampler,
+device, context or worker settings. `strata.json` remains the user's configuration.
+
+```text
+python tools/minimax/pack_gguf.py --model SHARD_DIRECTORY --model-root COMMON_MODEL_ROOT --companions COMPANION_DIRECTORY --out NEW_PACK_DIRECTORY --require-dspark
+```
+
+The explicit common root must contain the GGUF and companion files. File entries stay relative to
+that root, without `..`, UNC, ADS or escaped symlinks. Existing output is never overwritten.
+The output directory appears only after metadata preparation finishes. `.part` inputs, missing,
+short or inconsistent shards and missing required DSpark files are rejected.
+
+MiniMax-M3.1 runs sparse attention on all60layers. Missing first-layer indexers are errors;
+the tool never substitutes dense attention. Known MiniMax GGUF `minimax-m2` tokenizer labels
+are exported as the explicit Strata `minimax` scheme only for the matching model architecture
+and native vocabulary. This does not register other model architectures as MiniMax-M3.1.
+
+The OrcaRouter set also carries per-expert `.scale` vectors. llama.cpp passes these three role
+scales to its MoE graph ([reference6b95a99](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/6b95a99/src/models/minimax-m3.cpp)).
+Only vectors whose everyF32value is exactly1.0 may be omitted. Other values fail with an explicit
+error; role scales are never silently dropped or applied twice.
+
+The packer checks byte extents and metadata. This does not replace pinned SHA verification or
+qualification of model math, GPU graphs, MTP acceptance and throughput. The adapter is under
+integration; a successful metadata test is not a qualified runtime profile.
+
+`validate_pack.py` checks a completed pack against the original GGUF/safetensors headers and
+the completed producer/pack receipt. It checks every role's file, dtype, shape, offset and
+expert slice, sparse-indexer completeness and tokenizer identity. It hashes the small output
+metadata and checks pinned input size/mtime receipts; it does not rehash whole weights or
+execute the model. The receipt must have completed status; partial download states are refused.
+
+```text
+python tools/minimax/validate_pack.py --project-root PROJECT --pack PROJECT/packs/minimax-m31-mix128g --model-root PROJECT/weights --receipt PROJECT/research/current/minimax-20261102/pack-wait-status.json
+```
